               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 85-year-old female patient, admitted on 14th November 1973 with confirmed tubal ectopic pregnancy. On admission, clinical examination revealed acute lower abdominal pain with signs of peritoneal irritation. Transvaginal ultrasonography confirmed a right-sided tubal ectopic pregnancy with suspected early rupture. Laboratory investigations including serum beta-hCG and full blood count supported the diagnosis. Given the patient's clinical deterioration and surgical risk, the decision was made for urgent operative intervention. On 15th November 1973, the patient underwent laparoscopic salpingectomy for ectopic tubal pregnancy with uneventful intraoperative course. Postoperative recovery was satisfactory. The patient was discharged on 16th November 1973 in stable condition. Further gynaecological follow-up is recommended. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
